diff --git a/docs/TOML_SCHEMA.md b/docs/TOML_SCHEMA.md
index 8b95403..24ef0a9 100644
--- a/docs/TOML_SCHEMA.md
+++ b/docs/TOML_SCHEMA.md
@@ -493,3 +493,17 @@ Naming follows the sibling-recompiler convention:
 
 A future port of the TOML schema across recompilers should be
 straightforward.
+
+
+### Verified callback subtree frame boundary
+
+`[[jump_table]]` optionally accepts `defer_headless_frame_yield = true`
+(default false). Only that table's normalized target bodies receive an RAII
+`DeferHeadlessFrameYield` scope before their resume prologues. This preserves
+whole-interpreter-subtree headless stopping boundaries during qualified native
+migration. It does not alter instruction/device cycles, IRQ, debugger/HALT,
+presentation hooks or session scheduling. Interior resumes also enter the
+scope; returns/exceptions restore it. Missing independent target bodies or
+conflicting overlay scope settings fail generation. Requires runtime bridge
+patch support. Use only with measured migration evidence and unchanged full
+route gates; never to mask guest timing/fidelity defects or freeze all frames.
